    "description": "Commerce Platform calculates a cart total through a Checkout Pipeline. Customer Context identifies a region, loyalty tier, and active campaign, and these attributes can change between requests. The Pricing Engine currently contains conditionals for standard prices, member discounts, employee discounts, campaign pricing, tax handling, and fallback behavior. Each pricing variant must be selected at run time and must implement the same operation for producing a quote. The Checkout Pipeline must remain unaware of pricing details, and adding a campaign rule must not require recompiling or replacing the checkout workflow. The selected rule must receive an immutable pricing context, return line-level adjustments and a total, and participate in existing audit and metrics collection. Rule selection happens before quote calculation, with an explicit fallback used when no campaign rule matches. The team must choose how to organize the interchangeable pricing computations and how selection should be separated from the checkout flow.",
    "decision_statement": "Choose the structure that lets the Pricing Engine invoke interchangeable pricing computations selected from each Customer Context while keeping the Checkout Pipeline independent of rule details.",
    "notes": "Strategy fits the run-time selection of interchangeable pricing computations behind one quote operation; template-method is the near-miss (fixed calculation skeleton with varying steps). Differs from seed bs-pricing-strategy in system and variant axes (checkout cart vs tenant shipment pricing)."
